    "body": "Problem:\n`vim.str_byteindex(s, \"utf-8\", n)` looks like it converts Unicode code-point indices to byte indices, so `vim.str_byteindex(\"Слово\", \"utf-8\", 5)` returning `5` is surprising.\n\nSolution:\nDocument that `\"utf-8\"` is Nvim's native encoding (byte index in, byte index out) and that `\"utf-32\"` converts code-point indices to byte indices.\n\nFixes #35076",
    "closed_at": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "_links": {
                "html": {
                    "href": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41397#discussion_r3835624442"
                },
                "pull_request": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/41397"
                },
                "self": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/comments/3835624442"
                }
            },
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Basically fine but would change the order of the two sentences more or less. It is better to front with the user _should_ do.",
            "commit_id": "f77cfbb79388e90410baa7428a24e477b9aee403",
            "created_at": "2026-08-22T08:32:07Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -1468,6 +1468,11 @@ vim.str_byteindex({s}, {encoding}, {index}, {strict_indexing})\n     {strict_indexing} is false then an out of range index will return byte\n     length instead of throwing an error.\n \n+    `\"utf-8\"` is Nvim's native string encoding, so this function is idempotent\n+    for that encoding: {index} is already a byte index and is returned\n+    unchanged. It is not a Unicode code-point index. Use `\"utf-32\"` to convert\n+    code-point indices to byte indices.",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41397#discussion_r3835624442",
